{{~##
   The usings one generated file needs, decided by the writer rather than shared.

   It used to be one list every file got: an enum file opened with six namespaces and the
   binary reader to declare a handful of names, and none of them were reachable from it. The
   list is per file now - `usings` on the view - so what a file opens with is what it uses.

   No UniTask. There used to be a `using Cysharp.Threading.Tasks;` behind `#if !NO_UNITY`,
   and nothing in the generated code referenced it - so it bought a hard dependency on a
   third-party package, or a compile error for anyone without it, in exchange for nothing.
   The generated code awaits `Task`, which every platform has.
##~}}
{{~ for line in usings ~}}
{{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
